year after traumatic brain injury: A multi-center analysis</article-title><source>Arch Phys Med Rehabil</source><volume>78</volume><fpage>125</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9041891</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ndt-3-373"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wenden</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wade</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>The Rivermead head injury follow up questionnaire: a study of a new rating scale and other measures to evaluate outcome after head injury</article-title><source>J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry</source><volume>60</volume><fpage>510</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8778254</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ndt-3-373"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cummings</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mega</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>The neuropsychiatric inventory: comprehensive assessment of psychopathology in dementia</article-title><source>Neurology</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>2308</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7991117</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ndt-3-373"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deb</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>ICD-10 codes detect only a proportion of all head injury admissions</article-title><source>Brain Inj</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>369</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10367147</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ndt-3-373"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deb</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bryant</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Development and psychometric properties of the Carer-Head Injury Neurobehavioral Assessment Scale (C-HINAS) and the Carer-Head Injury Participation Scale (C-HIPS): patient and family determined outcome scales</article-title><source>Neuropsychiatr Dis Treat</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>389</fpage><lpage>408</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ndt-3-373"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deb</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyons</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Koutzoukis</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Neuropsychiatric sequelae one year after head injury</article-title><source>J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry</source><volume>65</volume><fpage>899</fpage><lpage>902</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9854967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ndt-3-373"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deb</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyons</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Koutzoukis</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999a</year><article-title>Neurobehavioural symptoms one year after head injury</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><volume>174</volume><fpage>360</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10533556</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ndt-3-373"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deb</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyons</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Koutzoukis</surname><given-nam